        "consequence": "The `queued` value is wrong and stale in every AssignmentSource instance, and it gets older the longer the process runs. Any logic or logging that relies on `queued` will see incorrect data.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "The dataclass field `queued: datetime = timezone.now()` calls `timezone.now()` once, when the class body runs at import. Every AssignmentSource built through `from_integration` gets that same import-time timestamp, not the time the assignment was queued. The field should use `field(default_factory=timezone.now)`.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "start_line": 18
        },
